# ACT ONE

## The Setup

= Margo's crew cases the pier on the last night of the season.

FADE IN:

EXT. SEASIDE AMUSEMENT PIER - NIGHT #1#

= The crew blends into the closing-night crowd.

Rain spits on the boardwalk. A Ferris wheel turns, half its bulbs dead. A thin crowd of TOURISTS hurries toward the exit while seagulls fight over a dropped funnel cake.

MARGO (30s), denim jacket, watchful, leans on the rail beside a coin-op telescope.

[[Need a practical rain rig for this one.]]

The carousel calliope WHEEZES out a waltz.

MARGO
(into her collar mic)
Lights on the wheel just went out. That's our *window*.

TEDDY (V.O.)
(over the radio)
Copy. I'm **parked** behind the funhouse.

/* An older version had Teddy waiting in a rowboat.
We cut it. */

MARGO
Five minutes. Then we're ghosts.

CUT TO:

EST. HARBOR LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT #2#

Fog rolls across the water. The beam sweeps the pier. [[VFX: the beam could be a practical.]]

INT./EXT. GETAWAY VAN - CONTINUOUS #2A#

TEDDY (50s), ski mask pushed up on his forehead, drums the steering wheel. A scruffy dog sleeps on the passenger seat.

A police car cruises past, siren off. Teddy sinks low.

TEDDY
(whispering)
Easy, Biscuit. Nobody's looking at us.

The dog THUMPS its tail.

TEDDY (CONT'D)
_Nobody_ ever looks at the van.

===

.INSIDE THE VAN

!SILENCE. Then the radio CRACKLES.

MARGO (O.S.)
Teddy. Now.

# ACT TWO

I/E. FUNHOUSE - MOMENTS LATER #3#

Margo slips through a service door. Mirrors stretch her into a dozen strangers. She pries open a panel with a crowbar and pulls out a BRASS KEY.

A security GUARD rounds the corner with a flashlight.

GUARD
Hey! Park's closed!

MARGO
So's my patience.

She leaps over the turnstile and sprints for the exit.

@McCLANE
You're not going anywhere.

INT. TICKET BOOTH - NIGHT #4#

Two teenagers argue over the last ticket roll.

BRODY
It's mine.

KIM ^
It's mine!

A jukebox in the corner plays "Moonlight on the Midway" as a firework BOOMS overhead. Smoke drifts past the window.

~Moonlight on the midway,
~meet me where the lights go down.

> FADE OUT.

>THE END<
